 * All ability components consider {{M|clones}}, {{M|illusions}}, and the {{H|Spirit Bear}} as heroes; other {{M|creep-heroes}} as creeps.
** Does not affect the following units:
*** {{M|Couriers}}

* {{Symbol|Projectile|Travel}}
** The {{M|projectile}} has {{Symbol|bonus cas}} {{#expr:{{#var:Spectral Dagger cast range}}/{{#var:Spectral Dagger basic1}}}}-second travel time to max distance.
** Has the following targeting functionalities:
*** {{Symbol|Target|Unit}}
**** When unit-targeted, the projectile homes in on the unit-targeted enemy hero, creating the Shadow Path until the projectile reaches the target.
**** Targeting units other than enemy heroes causes the ability to function as a {{Symbol|Target|Point}} point-targeted cast. 
*** {{Symbol|Target|Point}}
**** When point-targeted, the projectile does not home in on any enemy unit, and travels and creates the Shadow Path in a straight line. The travel distance is defined as:
***** {{cf|expr}} {{Code|TravelDistance {{=}} Ability[[Cast Range|CastRange]]}}

* The Shadow Path created has the following properties:
** The {{#var:Spectral Dagger type1 value2}}-second duration path duration begins upon the path segment's creation, not upon the ability cast.
** Spectral Daggers of different sources work independently of each other.
** {{Symbol|Vision|Flying}}
*** Each segment grants a non-lingering {{Symbol|bonus aoe}} 200-radius {{M|flying vision}} centered on the path radius.
** {{Symbol|Projectile|Travel}} {{to}} {{Symbol|Affect|Enemy}}
*** Applies two debuffs on all affected enemy units within {{Symbol|bonus aoe}} {{#var:Spectral Dagger value1}}-radius of the traveling dagger as follows:
**** [[File:Dota2 Condition-1.png|1|21px]] {{Symbol|Modifier|Debuff}} {{Code|spectre_spectral_dagger_in_path}}
***** The {{M|magical}} {{M|spell damage}}.
***** {{Symbol|Dispel|Any}}
****** [[Dispelling]] the debuff stops enemy heroes from creating and/or extending the path, but does not remove the already-created path.
**** [[File:Dota2 Condition-2.png|2|21px]] {{Symbol|Modifier|Debuff}} {{Code|spectre_spectral_dagger}}
***** The Path Creator debuff has the following properties:
****** Grants {{M|shared vision}} over affected enemy heroes.
****** Causes the debuff-affected enemy heroes to create additional Shadow Paths as they diverge.
** {{Symbol|Target|Area-Dummy}} {{Symbol|Aura}}
*** Each Shadow Path segment creates an [[aura]] and applies the following ability effects in 0.25-second intervals within its radius, starting immediately upon path creation:
**** {{Symbol|Modifier|Buff}} {{Code|spectre_spectral_dagger_in_path}} {{to}} {{Symbol|Affect|Self}} + {{Symbol|Affect|Enemy}}
***** Leveling up the ability immediately updates both the bonus and offensive {{M|movement speed}} values.
****** {{Symbol|Dispel|Any}}
******* Dispelling the debuff does not reapply the movement speed slow immediately.
******* Reapplies the debuff component when the affected enemy is affected by the aura component again.
***** The movement speed component applied has a {{#var:Spectral Dagger type2 value3}}-second linger duration upon leaving the path.
***** Reapplying the modifier of the same source refreshes its duration.
****** However, an offensive Spectral Dagger cast does not apply the {{M|movement speed}} slow debuff on Spectre while the buff is still active.
**** {{Symbol|Modifier|Buff}} {{Code|spectre_spectral_dagger_path_phased}} {{to}} {{Symbol|Affect|Self}}
***** Grants {{M|flying movement}} with a {{#var:Spectral Dagger type2 value2}}-second linger duration upon leaving the path.

{{Breaknotes
| name = Desolate
| desc = Does not affect the current Spectre's created [[illusions]].
}}

{{Breaknotes
| name = Desolate
| desc = Does not affect the current Spectre's created [[illusions]].
}}

 {{Gamedesc
| image = {{#var:Desolate icon0}}
| desc = Spectre and her illusions deal bonus Pure damage if attacking an enemy that does not have any allied units within a 350 radius around them.
}}
* {{Symbol|Target|Area-Dummy}}
** Checks if there are allied units of the attacked unit within the search radius.
*** There are currently 3 {{M|factions}} within the game: {{M|Radiant}}, {{M|Dire}}, and {{M|Neutral Creeps}}.
*** Attacking an enemy unit with a neutral unit within the radius, or vice versa, procs the ability effects, because these two units do not belong to the same faction.
*** Hence Spectre may proc all Desolate ability effects on when attacking an allied unit outside the search radius, in certain edge cases.

